          "content": {
            "id": "38de033c-7561-3459-9fe3-c0c0c87018fe",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Tether Is Shaking Up the Gold Market With Massive Metal Hoard",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Every week, more than a ton of gold is hauled in to the high-security vault, owned by crypto giant Tether Holdings SA, which is now the world\u2019s largest known hoard of bullion outside of banks and nation states.  Over the past year, Tether has quietly become one of the biggest players in the global gold market \u2014 the embodiment of a meeting of the crypto and gold worlds whose shared distrust of government debt is a major factor behind the surge in prices to never-before-seen highs above $5,200 an ounce.  When two of the most senior gold traders quit leading bullion bank HSBC Holdings Plc last year, the industry was abuzz with gossip about where they would head next; few guessed that the answer was Tether.",
